he append count while failing the visual placement requirement. | Add or revise an atomic work unit and step for the button stack layout, such as a `#button-chain-root button` or `.chain-button` style target, with acceptance criteria that every generated button appears below the prior current-last button. Map that work unit into the static and browser verification coverage. | open |\n| AR-03 | The plan claims \"test\" and \"automated\" proof in `plan-description.md` and `03-verification-handoff/goal.md`, but the inventory has no `test` work unit and no concrete automated test file/function or command. W04 is a static inspection verification, not an automated behavior test. | Either add a real test work unit with a named file/function or command and companion instructions, or revise the plan language to state that proof consists of bounded static inspection plus browser story verification only. The work-unit inventory, goal text, and acceptance coverage must use one consistent testing model. | open |\n| AR-04 | The UI bug-recovery path is under-specified for the mandatory UI story workflow. The plan says failures go into `bugs.md` and need investigation/fix goals, but it does not require changing `US-01` to `🐛 bug found`, recording browser reproduction evidence, adding both `NN-investigate-...` and `NN-fix-...` goals before fixes, updating the inventory/progress/story artifacts, and rerunning affected stories before completion. | Expand the browser-story verification and bug-register instructions to mirror the UI reference: on failure, mark the story `🐛 bug found`, record reproduction/evidence/severity, create investigation and fix goals with new work units, update `bugs.md`, `ui-user-stories.md`, progress trackers, and the inventory before execution resumes, then retest `US-01` and dependent stories. | open |\n\n## Verdict\n\n- Status: not approved\n- Rationale: The plan captures the main future behavior, including the fourth-generated-button terminal condition, but it is not ready under the benchmark and UI-planning contracts until AR-01 through AR-04 are resolved and the review is rerun.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
