{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T210953Z-pilot-142-control-isolated-plan/adversarial-review.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial review: basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T210953Z-pilot-142-control-isolated-plan\n\n## Verdict\n\nnot approved\n\nThis is a fresh independent review based only on the allowed benchmark/specification inputs, the tagged planning skill and UI validation reference, and the current plan directory excluding any prior `adversarial-review.md` content. No HTML file, browser, server, driver, or test execution was inspected or created.\n\n## Findings\n\n### AR-01 - Required final validation/report artifact is missing from the planned work\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: `benchmark-test.md` requires the plan itself to contain a substantive `validation.md` produced by the final tagged validator run before final completion, and the harness gate expects validation/analysis report artifacts. `plan-description.md` says readiness requires \"a passing tagged validator result\", but the plan directory has no `validation.md`, no analysis/report artifact, and no work unit or step that creates or records the final tagged validator result inside the plan.\n\nRequired change: Add explicit plan work for the final tagged validator run and its durable report artifact, including the expected `validation.md` contents/status and any benchmark-facing analysis or handoff report required before completion.\n\n### AR-02 - Verification work units do not name executable commands\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: The planning skill defines verification work units as one named command or one bounded browser/API flow. `W07`, `W08`, and `W04` are described as \"Document shell source inspection\", \"Chain behavior source inspection\", and \"Static acceptance inspection command\", but their step instructions say only to run a bounded source inspection of `button-chain.html` or `handleChainClick(event)`. They do not provide concrete commands, expected inputs, or output shape for the future executor to run and record.\n\nRequired change: Replace the generic inspection language with exact bounded command lines or clearly specified command recipes and pass/fail output requirements for each static verification unit.\n\n### AR-03 - UI run cache is not decomposed into the required action sequence\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` records all five clicks as a single order row. The UI validation reference requires caching every action in execution order, its target/value, and every wait/readiness check. The current cache does not give separate rows for the initial button, generated button 1, generated button 2, generated button 3, and generated button 4, so a future browser run cannot execute the cache exactly without re-planning the interaction.\n\nRequired change: Split `US-01` into separate ordered cached inputs and readiness rows for each required visible click, preserving the direct-interaction rule and terminal expected result.\n\n### AR-04 - UI story coverage omits the layout work unit it verifies\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: `ui-user-stories.md` says `US-01` verifies that each appended button appears below the current last button, but its related work units are `W01,W02,W03,W05`. The below-placement behavior is owned by `W06` in `work-unit-inventory.md`, so the story-to-work-unit mapping is incomplete.\n\nRequired change: Add `W06` to `US-01` related work units and ensure the final browser verification step treats below-placement as a direct acceptance point.\n\n### AR-05 - Bug recovery path allows untracked corrections before the required investigation/fix loop\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: `01-document-shell/steps/04-step-verify-document-shell.md` says any failure is \"entered in `bugs.md` or corrected before `W03` starts.\" The UI validation reference requires failed stories and unexpected bugs to be recorded, traced to investigation and fix goals, and retested; verification steps must not make fixes. The \"or corrected\" path permits untracked repair without new work units, goals, progress updates, or bug evidence.\n\nRequired change: Remove the untracked correction option from verification steps. Require failed verification to be recorded and handled through explicit investigation/fix work units or through a clearly scoped plan revision before execution continues.\n\n### AR-06 - Goal owned-work-unit sections are malformed and duplicated\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: `01-document-shell/goal.md` lists `W01` under \"Owned work units\", then inserts the testing requirement table before `W02`, `W06`, and `W07`. It also duplicates `W06` and `W07` paragraphs. `02-chain-behavior/goal.md` duplicates `W08`. This weakens the one-to-one goal/step ownership record and may make validator or executor interpretation unreliable.\n\nRequired change: Normalize each goal so the \"Owned work units\" section contains each owned ID exactly once, the testing requirement appears only in the testing section, and paragraph numbering is stable.\n\n### AR-07 - Progress trackers still contain placeholder descriptions\n\nStatus: open\n\nEvidence: The plan-level `progress.md` and all goal-level progress files use `<short description>` for goals and steps. The benchmark and planning skill require resumable progress trackers; placeholder descriptions do not give a future executor or analyzer meaningful progress evidence.\n\nRequired change: Replace all placeholder descriptions with concise descriptions matching the actual goal and step outcomes.\n\n## Positive evidence\n\n- The plan preserves the planning-only boundary: the artifacts state that no HTML, browser, server, driver, or UI execution tooling was created or used during this proof.\n- The core future behavior is identified: one initial button, current-last-button append behavior, terminal action on the fourth generated button, exact lowercase `finished`, and a visible white border.\n- The plan includes a UI classification, UI story artifact, bug register, run cache, work-unit inventory, goal directories, step files, and testing companions.\n- The future browser verification is planned as direct user-facing clicks rather than console, DOM mutation, storage edit, direct API, or injected-event shortcuts.\n\n## Required changes before approval\n\nResolve AR-01 through AR-07, rerun the tagged plan validator, add the durable validation/report artifact expected by the benchmark, and then request a fresh independent adversarial review. The review status in `plan-description.md` must remain pending until an approved review artifact exists.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
